          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Writing Style and Techniques</strong><br>\nFamous for his detail-oriented and exhaustive depictions of reality, Balzac's writing style is considered a precursor to realism in European literature. He meticulously researched for his novels, creating a vast and vivid cast of characters.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Balzac's Themes</strong><br>\nHis works often explored themes of social climbing, the influence of money on people, and the intricacies of family and social ties. Balzac was a keen observer of his era and its people, which he demonstrated through his writings.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Personal and Financial Struggles</strong><br>\nThroughout his career, Balzac faced significant financial challenges, in part because of his lavish lifestyle and business misadventures. His dedication to writing was partly driven by the need to pay off debts.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
